From f942cbb69e3c8d5b1fd6e8b51b5a39074ba32324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:17:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] kde: repaint the owed region on buffer catch-up before
 KWin 6.6

When the consumer selects a rotation buffer that still owes damage,
scheduleBufferCatchUp() asks the compositor to run. KWin 6.6 has
per-layer scheduleRepaint(), but older KWin only gets
renderLoop()->scheduleRepaint(), which runs a frame without marking the
layer dirty. KWin then presents without painting, presentFrame() commits
the selected slot, and its stale content reaches the screen.

The visible result is that every fade blinks: a closing window or the
Plasma splash toggles on and off once per rotation buffer before it is
gone. Instrumenting KWin 6.3.6 (Debian 13) showed 119 commits without a
render out of about 3000 frames, all on catch-up.

Add the slot's accumulated damage as layer damage before scheduling, so
the catch-up frame actually repaints it. After the change the same
session committed 2396 frames from 2396 renders and the blinking is gone.

Signed-off-by: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
---
 .../src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp             | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/producers/kde/anland_backend/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp b/producers/kde/anland_backend/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp
index 251d835..30c8b20 100644
--- a/producers/kde/anland_backend/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp
+++ b/producers/kde/anland_backend/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp
@@ -285,7 +285,12 @@ void AnlandEglLayer::scheduleBufferCatchUp(int index)
         // KWin 6.6 added per-layer repaint scheduling.
         scheduleRepaint(nullptr);
 #else
-        // Older KWin versions schedule the compositor through the render loop.
+        // Older KWin versions schedule the compositor through the render loop,
+        // which runs a frame without marking this layer dirty. KWin then
+        // presents without painting and the slot's stale content reaches the
+        // screen: fades blink once per rotation buffer. Turn the owed region
+        // into layer damage so the frame actually repaints it.
+        addRepaint(m_accumDamage[index]);
         m_output->renderLoop()->scheduleRepaint();
 #endif
     }
